config FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ_DDS238
	bool "Domoticz plugin: DDS238 energy meter (Modbus RS-485)"
	depends on FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ
	select FREETZ_PACKAGE_PYTHON3_PYSERIAL
	default n
	help
		readings of the DDS238 energy meters and of the devices that speak the same Modbus protocol (it ships its own copy of minimalmodbus and uses pyserial for the RS-485 port).

		It is a Python plugin of Domoticz: the package installs it into
		/usr/share/domoticz/plugins/domoticz-dds238, the directory Domoticz is
		started with (-approot of the domoticz package), and it needs no
		change of the Domoticz build.

		Setup -> Hardware -> DDS238, enter the serial port, the Modbus address and the model.

		Licensed upstream (LICENSE is installed with the plugin). The
		repository has no release tags, so the build fetches a pinned commit of
		the default branch.
